[{"role": "system", "content": "You are proposing causal mechanics for a governed world model. Return exactly one JSON object and no prose or markdown. You are not writing code. mechanics must hold one mechanic for each of these moves: stack-chair, carry-tray, pick-up-tray, right-tray, mop-floor, brew-coffee, sip-coffee, request-coffee, knock-over; an empty mechanics list is always rejected. The response must satisfy response_contract. Every effect must be justified by represented state and the action description. Prefer conservative refusal checks over assumptions. Do not add reads/writes fields; the local compiler derives authority. Whenever you name a state path, copy it EXACTLY from allowed_state_paths. Where one change physically sets off another at once (a fall, a break, a spill, a noise heard nearby), write that consequence as a process with timing immediately."}, {"role": "user", "content": "{
  "actions": [
