[{"role": "system", "content": "You read the recorded events of one finished simulation and say plainly what happened, through a fixed lens. Use only the events given; never invent an event. For each mechanism, say present only when you can cite at least one event_id from the list that shows it, and name the events that show it best (at most eight). Otherwise say missing and give the plain reason (for example: nobody's support ever depended on a condition; no settled item was ever undone). Write for someone who has never seen the simulation: short sentences, the people's names, no ids in the prose. Return only JSON: {"summary": str (two or three sentences on what happened overall), "mechanisms": [{"id": str, "status": "present" | "missing", "event_ids": [str], "explanation": str (one or two sentences), "missing_reason": str (empty when present)}]}."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Lens: How goods moved through the chain
Mechanisms:
- goods-made: Goods made from other goods. Someone turns inputs into a new kind of good (for example logs into boards), using the inputs up.
- goods-handed-on: Goods carried to the next step. Someone moves goods from one place or business to another, where the next step uses them.
- demand-met: Demand reached and met. Finished goods reach the place that wants them and are taken or used there.
- work-waited: Work held up. A step could not go ahead because what it needs had not arrived or had run out, so someone waited or the chain stalled.

People:
- (not recorded)

Events (32, in order):
